  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The work done will be against surface tension and we know that surface tension is related to work as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>×</mo><mo>∆</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math><br />Since, the surface area of sphere is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>πR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;and there are two free surfaces, we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><msup><mi>πR</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; ...<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br />and volume of sphere <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>πR</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math></p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>πR</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp; &nbsp;...<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br /><br />From Eqs.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, we get<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mo>×</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>∝</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∝</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msubsup></math><br /><br />and,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∝</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msubsup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi></math></p>",
